1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,380
Turn on the light and try leaving me.

2
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
Someone who goes home right
after the night is over.

4
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:47,359
Don't rush.
Where are you going in this narrow town?

5
00:00:47,409 --> 00:00:49,380
Haste makes waste.

6
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:58,520
If, by any chance,
there's someone better than me,

7
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:03,020
tell me about it. Tell me all night long.

8
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:12,820
I don't mind waiting.

9
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:17,020
Because I'm a Kame-za woman.

10
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,700
I won't lose to a Ginza woman.

11
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:26,520
I'll love you for years and years.

12
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:29,860
The everyday life of a Kame-za woman.

13
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,420
Where there's laughter, there's Ebisu-kun.

14
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:49,060
Ryo-chan, what are you making this time?

15
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:52,100
It's a wooden mold for a TV character doll.

16
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:55,780
Until the other day you were making wooden grips for a model gun,
weren't you?

17
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:58,280
That took too much work, so I quit.

18
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,980
With character items,
if you make just one resin mold

19
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:06,540
you can make money. This month I'm
staking my whole livelihood on this.

20
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,180
But you really do carve so skillfully.

21
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:12,778
Back when I was a kid,
I was a pencil-sharpening genius.

22
00:02:12,828 --> 00:02:14,080
I can make anything.

23
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:17,420
Then how about Hokkaido bear souvenirs?

24
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,780
I can do it in five minutes.
The Chief's face, I can do in two.

25
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:22,960
In two minutes?

26
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,362
Just watch.

27
00:02:24,412 --> 00:02:28,320
Nothing is impossible for me,
the Michelangelo of Kameari.

28
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:33,620
There, it's done!

29
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,000
W-wow!

30
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,960
And it looks just like him!

31
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,700
Didn't I tell you I'm a genius?

32
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,120
Maybe I should add a bit more expression.

33
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:46,120
Uh, hngh...

34
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,040
Make the eyes look a little more sinister.

35
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,960
Should the space under the nose be longer?

36
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,860
Phew, there, it's finished!

37
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:52,760
Heh heh.

38
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:56,440
It's dripping with the Chief's nasty vibe!

39
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,560
Hehehehehehe.

40
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,780
The original nasty guy?

41
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,140
Who's nasty?

42
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:06,360
I said "cool." A cool, handsome guy.

43
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,462
What are these wood shavings?

44
00:03:10,512 --> 00:03:13,080
You were up to something again, Ryotsu.

45
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:16,920
No, this is katsuobushi. Katsuobushi.

46
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,500
Then eat it.

47
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,900
It's katsuobushi, right?

48
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:26,620
That's right. This katsuobushi
is the most delicious there is.

49
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,420
Eat all of it. Don't leave a scrap.

50
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,780
Of course.

51
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,160
Ryo-chan

52
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,260
You don't have to force yourself that much.

53
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,080
Mai-mai.

54
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:40,300
By the way, Nakagawa, Reiko.

55
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:44,320
Today I brought in a rookie who's been transferred
from the detective division to the station.

56
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:46,700
Hey, Ebisu, come in.

57
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:47,600
Yes!

58
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:53,940
Hello, everyone.
I'm Ebisu. Nice to meet you.

59
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,040
I'm Nakagawa. Likewise.

60
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:58,860
I'm Reiko Akimoto.

61
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,840
What a lucky name.

62
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:02,480
Yes.

63
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:06,640
Well, you've already got the greeting down.
Now eat up.

64
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,380
Too loud!

65
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,200
Cold water!

66
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:15,340
Yes.

67
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,200
Here's your water, Ryo-chan.

68
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,920
Sorry for startling you.

69
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,620
What is wrong with you?

70
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,080
Laughing out of nowhere like that!

71
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,460
Sorry, sorry, really.

72
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:31,680
I'm the laughing type.

73
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,940
There's laughing,
and then there's too much of it!

74
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,946
You see, I come from a cheerful family,

75
00:04:38,996 --> 00:04:41,690
so there was always
laughter since I was a kid,

76
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,800
and now my smiling face
won't go back to normal.

77
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,360
Being cheerful is a good thing, isn't it?

78
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,834
It's too cheerful, it's a problem.

79
00:04:49,884 --> 00:04:53,220
Whenever I try to be serious,
it just makes me laugh even more.

80
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:57,600
Ebisu, why did you go
from detective to patrol?

81
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,920
Yes, with a personality like this,
I wasn't cut out for detective work.

82
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,380
Hey, look, it's katsuobushi!

83
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,300
You must be hungry.
Eat that, and you'd better confess properly.

84
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:16,600
This is where the action comes in, I guess.
What about Ebisu?

85
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:23,820
But you're going to talk about his hometown and his mom,
then make him do some action, right?

86
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,920
W-what is this guy?

87
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,080
N-no way.

88
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:30,040
Come on, enough already.

89
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:31,120
Yes.

90
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:35,020
And that's how it ended up.

91
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,660
Then he's not cut out
to be a detective, is he?

92
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,580
Seriously.

93
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:42,580
We really got a piece of work here, Chief.

94
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,000
Well then, straight to business. Ryotsu.

95
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,320
Go on patrol with Ebisu.

96
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,420
Wait, I have to go with him?

97
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:52,260
Of course. You're going to train him.

98
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,100
Training

99
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,660
Nice to meet you. Please take care of me.

100
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:01,080
Here we go again.

101
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,580
Stop laughing and let's go on patrol.

102
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,160
Patrol, he says?

103
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,920
This guy's hopeless.

104
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:10,200
Come on, let's go.

105
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,760
Come on, pull yourself together. Let's go.

106
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,980
Walk properly.

107
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:20,140
Sorry, I just can't get
any strength into my body.

108
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,740
What a troublesome guy.

109
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:31,120
This wasn't a joke! Is this team going to be all right? That guy...
I agreed to it because I figured that if we left it to Ryotsu, it would somehow work out.

110
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,580
Even Ryo-chan might find this hard.

111
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:45,340
Hey, what's so funny this time?
This isn't patrol. Sorry.

112
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,940
It's that car's fault.

113
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,900
What's wrong with the Volkswagen Beetle?

114
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:59,320
Just imagining it driving around in that shape,
it's so funny, so funny.

115
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,620
Don't laugh at trivial things.

116
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:05,560
I'm laughing so hard it hurts.
Please help me.

117
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,860
Deal with it yourself. I don't know.

118
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,820
Though I used to laugh at
things that were actually funny.

119
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:18,380
But lately it's indiscriminate.
It's really troublesome.

120
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,080
I'm the one who's in trouble here.

121
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,580
If you're like this,
what happens if you go listen to rakugo?

122
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:29,080
Well, just seeing the sign
outside the performance hall.

123
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,900
"Suspicious" is Kobue, you know.

124
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,480
Why is it named Kobue?

125
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Sorry, I'm laughing so hard.

126
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:39,840
Just kidding.

127
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,000
That's how it goes,
so it's really a bad habit.

128
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:56,320
Then who knows what would happen. If your father Sanpei were alive, you'd have laughed yourself to death.
Even just touching a Shonen Jump manga, I laugh for two hours.

129
00:07:57,140 --> 00:08:04,960
So you've had your share of hardship. I was raised to believe that fortune
comes to those who laugh at the corners. I resent my parents for that.

130
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:12,820
What's with the sudden laughing?

131
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:15,860
Sorry, I can't stop.

132
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:20,300
Are you mocking me? Cut it out!

133
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:24,820
Hey, what's wrong with you?

134
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,460
I laughed at someone's face and got punched.

135
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:32,060
Well, of course.
People in the old town have short fuses.

136
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:34,520
Stop looking around and follow me.

137
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,320
Sorry, whenever our eyes meet,
I just end up laughing.

138
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:43,000
An accident!

139
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:45,680
Are you okay?

140
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,300
Somehow.

141
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:50,600
Are you all right?

142
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,680
Don't laugh.

143
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,760
I'm sorry.

144
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,500
Officer, excuse me, but this is...

145
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:01,500
Could you deliver this to
the Onigahara house up ahead?

146
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:02,940
Alright, I understand.

147
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:06,040
Here he comes. Hey, Ebisu.
Take this death notice over.

148
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:08,245
N-no way.

149
00:09:08,295 --> 00:09:11,520
I can't go to a funeral with this face.

150
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,887
Just keep your head down
and hand it over in silence.

151
00:09:14,937 --> 00:09:16,960
I'll be attending the
accident investigation.

152
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,240
B-but...

153
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,340
Hurry up and go!

154
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,280
Y-yes, sir!

155
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:28,940
Damn it.

156
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:32,100
Tense situations like
this are my worst weakness.

157
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:33,840
No good.

158
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,320
But it's my first job
since I was cleared for duty.

159
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:38,240
I have to hold it in somehow.

160
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:47,680
Sorry, thank you.

161
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:48,940
No, the pleasure is mine.

162
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,660
N-nothing, it's nothing.

163
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,440
This way.

164
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:59,001
Th-thanks,

165
00:09:59,051 --> 00:10:01,840
My condolences on your loss.

166
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,500
Thank you for your kindness.

167
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:08,560
Hey Mom, that monk looked like he was dozing off,
didn't he?

168
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:11,880
Well then.

169
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,540
The incense offering is over there.

170
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:16,040
No

171
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,620
I never expected you to cry so much.

172
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:25,700
That's right.

173
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,900
I'm finished.

174
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,160
For goodness' sake.

175
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,940
Luckily, the injuries weren't too serious.

176
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:49,000
Speaking of which, Ebisu is taking forever.

177
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,740
Sorry I'm late.

178
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,820
What's with that face?
Did you get punched again?

179
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,471
Sigh, I guess except for happy occasions,

180
00:10:59,521 --> 00:11:02,300
I always get disapproving looks, don't I?
It's this face of mine.

181
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,800
Honestly, you're hopeless.

182
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,460
This is no laughing matter, you know.

183
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,500
Sorry.

184
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:30,340
Even Ryotsu couldn't handle him

185
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:33,460
It's like walking around with a bomb.

186
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,120
But if he can't even go on patrol...

187
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:38,300
Working at the police box will be tough,
won't it?

188
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,320
One more place.

189
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:44,160
What's wrong, Ebisu?

190
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:46,060
Stop grinning and speak clearly.

191
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:49,300
Actually, I think I'm about to leak.

192
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,980
The toilet's in the back,
hurry up and go take a leak.

193
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,380
Hurry up and go take a leak.

194
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:00,860
That's insane.

195
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:10,020
Look, who laughs at the Chief's dad
jokes that freeze everyone over like that?

196
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:12,720
But it was so damn funny!

197
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:16,500
It was that funny?

198
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:17,935
So then,

199
00:12:17,985 --> 00:12:21,700
"Saw Tokyo Tower and was astonished,
haha, get it?"

200
00:12:21,980 --> 00:12:25,460
Hahahaha, it hurts!
My stomach's about to twist up!

201
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:26,720
Hahahaha.

202
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:27,560
Hey.

203
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:30,700
Hahahaha.

204
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:34,320
Hey, Reiko! You don't have to laugh too!

205
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,860
But Ebisu-san's laughing so
much that I finally just...!

206
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:38,880
Hahahaha.

207
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:44,540
My gags have been mocked endlessly by the kids,
and now they're getting this big a laugh?

208
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:45,940
This is absolutely the best.

209
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:48,440
I can't take it anymore.

210
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,700
Hey, stop laughing! You'll only make
the old man even more full of himself.

211
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,140
Easier said than done.

212
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:56,760
Ebisu-san,
don't you need to go to the bathroom?

213
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,680
That's right.

214
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:02,960
Since it's about "pee,
" I'll say "pee"... just kidding!

215
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,020
I'm just going to go to sleep already.

216
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:12,800
What is going on here?

217
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,020
Oh no, what's wrong with me?

218
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,800
They say laughter is contagious, after all.

219
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:28,780
Looks like Ebisu's laughter brings
good fortune to those around him, too.

220
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:32,840
Laughing at rotten dad jokes like
that won't bring any good fortune.

221
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,680
What did you say?

222
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,340
Just kidding.

223
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:40,180
Wait, even if patrol's out,
this guy might still be useful.

224
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,160
I almost peed myself.

225
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:50,600
Ebisu, would you come
to the station with me?

226
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:53,860
Chief, what are you going there for?

227
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:55,520
None of your business.

228
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:58,480
Then, Nakagawa and Reiko,
the rest is in your hands.

229
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,060
Yes.

230
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:04,420
Suspicious... I smell something fishy.

231
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,620
I'm heading out too.

232
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,480
Senpai.

233
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,100
It's Ryo-chan now, right?

234
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,280
It's Chief-chan now, right?

235
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:19,840
Well then, how about this one?

236
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:22,900
Friday, today's side dish is Fry-day!

237
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:29,680
Saturday, long time no see,
I'm back after a while, hehe.

238
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,100
That's ridiculous.

239
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:37,540
Sunday, today it's kids' meals until noon.

240
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:42,580
Why is such a dad joke so funny?

241
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:43,880
Really, really.

242
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,940
Monday, I don't read anything but Jump.

243
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:49,320
Just as I thought.

244
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:53,100
He's using Ebisu to crack up
the parents with dad jokes!

245
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:59,000
Ohara, what's all this racket about?

246
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,340
Chief, well, actually...

247
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:06,400
No matter what joke you tell, he cracks up.
Is that true?

248
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:06,836
Yes,

249
00:15:06,886 --> 00:15:10,620
As long as Ebisu-kun is here,
you're guaranteed a big hit.

250
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:13,880
Why don't you try one yourself, Chief?

251
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:15,680
W-well, really?

252
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:22,240
Then here's one: I forgot my hat, and I got a real
"ha-t" shock!

253
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:28,340
It landed!
After all the mocking I've taken until now!

254
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:31,780
See? Just like I said, right?

255
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:36,960
I'll do one more too: on Wednesday, I'll plant a tree in the garden...
Wed-nes-day!

256
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,840
I can't stop!

257
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:42,900
It hurts!

258
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:48,340
Thursday, if it rains, I'll put up my umbrella...
Thurs-day!

259
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:52,260
I'm dying, I'm dying!

260
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,220
Splendid, Ohara-kun!

261
00:15:55,220 --> 00:16:00,540
Getting big laughs from a dad
joke as old as the Stone Age

262
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:02,280
I can't take it anymore!

263
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,100
Chief, President

264
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,280
Rose

265
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:10,240
Is it really okay for a police officer
to keep spouting dad jokes on duty?

266
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,580
So you want to get laughs with jokes too

267
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,340
No, that's not it.

268
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:18,760
You're just jealous because we're getting such big laughs,
aren't you?

269
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,160
Right, Ohara-kun?

270
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:21,820
That's right, Chief.

271
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,180
That's not true at all.

272
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:26,020
And Ebisu, you're no better yourself!

273
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:27,120
Come here for a sec.

274
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,900
My stomach hurts too much to eat.

275
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,320
Let's eat.

276
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,720
We were having such a great laugh.

277
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:37,940
Chief, it's fine.

278
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:41,220
Our gags hit everyone's funny bone.

279
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,920
Even without Ebisu, we're doing just fine.

280
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:45,540
Yeah, that's right.

281
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:48,000
Then, once more, one more joke.

282
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:50,600
The train announcement said this:

283
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:53,880
"Please wait a while until we reach Chiba."

284
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:58,580
Such a lame, terrible dad joke.

285
00:16:58,580 --> 00:16:59,400
Seriously.

286
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:01,740
Hello there.

287
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,920
"Just wait a while, ha-ha, just kidding."

288
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,760
It's no fun at all without Snake-san.

289
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,620
Come on, everyone, let's go, let's go.

290
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:15,380
So,

291
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:17,660
You didn't join the force

292
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:20,480
to flatter the Chief and the station head,
did you?

293
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,480
Well,

294
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,580
to protect the citizens' safety

295
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:25,080
and fight evil, right?

296
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:25,820
Yes.

297
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:28,040
Then never laugh again.

298
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:32,760
That's impossible.
It's like being told not to breathe.

299
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:36,316
Shut up! Besides,
if a cop goes around grinning like an idiot,

300
00:17:36,366 --> 00:17:38,580
citizens won't trust him, will they?

301
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:42,480
Excuse me,
I'd like to ask you for directions.

302
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,900
Yes, yes, what is it, grandma?

303
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:47,143
What's your problem, you?

304
00:17:47,193 --> 00:17:50,620
What's so funny about grinning like
an idiot when people are in trouble?

305
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,129
You, officer over there,

306
00:17:53,179 --> 00:17:56,080
is there a Sky Mansion around here?

307
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:58,860
That's the brick-colored
building over there.

308
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:03,380
That one? Thank you, officer.

309
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:07,160
Look at that! This is what happens
when you go around grinning like that!

310
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:11,070
Listen, don't you dare laugh!
If you can't manage that,

311
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,720
then just quit the police force!

312
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:23,680
I guess I'm just not cut out for the police

313
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,120
I resent my parents for
giving me this Ebisu face.

314
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,700
I should be depressed,
but I'm still smiling.

315
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,220
Ugh, I'm hopeless.

316
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:43,040
Just quit the police already!

317
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:51,320
Sir, something terrible has happened!

318
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:54,160
Robbers broke in and took
a female employee hostage!

319
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,080
Robbers!

320
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,500
You can't laugh at a time like this!

321
00:18:59,560 --> 00:18:59,880
Right.

322
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:03,160
What? At the loan shark on Fourth Street?

323
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:05,680
The robbers are holed up in there with them?

324
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,200
Got it.

325
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,000
I'm on my way.

326
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:10,100
Nakagawa, come with me.

327
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,380
Reiko, contact the station.

328
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:18,400
Ebisu

329
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,120
Senpai

330
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:21,380
How many culprits are there?

331
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:23,980
Just one, but he has a handgun.

332
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:26,880
Just one?
Leave it to me, I'll talk him down.

333
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,580
Hey, criminal! It's the police!

334
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,960
This building is already surrounded.

335
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,020
You can't escape.

336
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,000
Give up and come out quietly. Surrender.

337
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:36,480
Shut up!

338
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,340
We've got a hostage here!

339
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:40,060
I'm not getting caught that easily!

340
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:42,300
Going in there would be dangerous.

341
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:44,140
Damn it, any good ideas?

342
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:48,800
Alright, let Ebisu talk him down.

343
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,560
Me? Really?

344
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:54,920
You're the laugh-prone one.
If you talk him down while laughing,

345
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,700
Nakagawa and I will handle
it while he's distracted.

346
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,980
But you told me not to laugh earlier!

347
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,400
Just go already.

348
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:05,840
Go!

349
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,860
Who the hell are you?

350
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,860
I'm here to talk you down.

351
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:13,440
Who are you?

352
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:16,080
Under this extreme tension,
I can't help but laugh.

353
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:21,020
You damn clown.

354
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:23,480
If you laugh any more, I'll put a hole
Translation>
in this guy's head.

355
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,540
I think they call that a bullet hole, right?

356
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:26,440
At a time like this,

357
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:29,940
don't you dare laugh! I'm serious!

358
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:31,800
But you're telling me that...

359
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:33,940
I'm telling you not to laugh!

360
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,240
But it's just so funny, so funny...

361
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:43,040
N-no way...
you knew this display was a model gun...

362
00:20:43,540 --> 00:20:44,100
Damn it!

363
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:48,160
W-what, it was a model gun all along...

364
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:51,640
So that's why you were laughing, right?

365
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:54,060
Stupid criminal!

366
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:55,900
Don't you dare laugh, hostage too!

367
00:20:57,780 --> 00:21:01,860
Damn it! I still have an ace up my sleeve!
Look at this!

368
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,020
Dynamite!

369
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,960
Damn it! We can't rush in like this!

370
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:08,880
He even went and got dynamite!

371
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:13,500
But he forgot the lighter,
so he couldn't light the fuse!

372
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:20,100
I-I forgot it...

373
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:20,820
Hey!

374
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:26,320
He really forgot it! I'm splitting my sides!

375
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:29,200
Help me!

376
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,440
Stop laughing and mocking me any more!

377
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,920
I've been telling you to stop!

378
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,420
Alright, now!

379
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:36,260
What?

380
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:39,080
If it's a dud, we've got the upper hand!

381
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:40,360
Durian!

382
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:48,660
Are you all right?

383
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:49,560
Yes.

384
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:52,320
We did it, senpai.

385
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:52,680
Yeah.

386
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:55,400
It's all thanks to Ebisu-san.

387
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:58,820
It's hopeless.

388
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:02,820
He fainted from laughing too much, damn him.

389
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:05,060
He really is an amazing guy, isn't he.

390
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,280
Ebisu quit?

391
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,120
After he went and earned
such a great achievement, why?

392
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:18,120
So he gave up, deciding he couldn't be a
police officer with that laughing habit of his.

393
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:23,420
Actually, he only quit working at the police box.
He didn't quit the police.

394
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:24,020
What?

395
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,986
After hearing about
Ebisu's exploits yesterday,

396
00:22:27,036 --> 00:22:30,220
a department came asking
very eagerly for him.

397
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:34,000
As of today,
he's been assigned to your section.

398
00:22:34,420 --> 00:22:38,120
Who'd have thought anyone would want
to hire that comedy bomb of a man!

399
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:45,080
That laugh... could it be?

400
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,020
The bulge in my crotch isn't just for show.

401
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:52,130
When trouble strikes on land,

402
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:54,340
it's all solved with just
a pair of swim trunks!

403
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:58,460
Leader of the Special Criminal Investigation Unit Samba Glass,
Kaipan Deka!

404
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:04,100
Long time no see,
master of the Kameari Park police box.

405
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:07,780
So it's you, Kaipan Deka.
What on earth are you doing here?

406
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:13,760
Actually, a new member has joined the Special Criminal Investigation Unit,
so I came to introduce him.

407
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,320
A new member.

408
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,500
Come in, Laughing Deka!

409
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,100
Hello, everyone.

410
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,520
Isn't that Ebisu?

411
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:30,000
Who was it that asked for Ebisu?

412
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:32,580
Of course,
our Special Criminal Investigation Unit.

413
00:23:33,740 --> 00:23:35,860
We do our jobs dressed like this.

414
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:37,920
I can't believe it.

415
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:40,880
I just can't stop.

416
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:43,000
That's how it is.

417
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:47,720
There's no place but here that would want Ebisu,
is there?

418
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,200
Count on you, Laughing Deka.

419
00:23:51,820 --> 00:23:53,420
Yes, Senior Kaipan.

420
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:14,780
Within the seasons that gently drift past

421
00:24:15,780 --> 00:24:19,520
I've gotten good at forced smiles.

422
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:24,880
Swept along and changing, I wonder

423
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:29,220
how I appear in your eyes.

424
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:36,120
After every fight,
we always share a brief kiss.

425
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:40,240
You, with your teary eyes,
were so dear to me.

426
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:45,460
Like that, the irreplaceable things

427
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:50,900
how many could a person
ever hold in a lifetime?

428
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:57,260
You are me, and I am you,

429
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:02,260
and that alone was enough to fill me.

430
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:08,420
Just seeing you smile

431
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:15,020
made every hardship feel healed.

432
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,000
A card battle? Now that's interesting!

433
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,720
Alright, go call everyone!

434
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,560
It's a grand card tournament!

435
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:32,400
Wait, don't tell me this whole anime
is just 30 minutes of playing cards!

436
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:36,720
Next time: Battle, Trump Shimokunijo!
See you then!

